Wait — how do I find what content was written? file_write(p, c) — pushes path and content. Collect into a map/array.

Expected content for matched BA item:
- Title: '# Business Analysis — [BA] Some Title\n'
- blockquote: '> **Business Analysis** (PROJ-200): BA desc\n'
- '**Ticket:** PROJ-200\n**Status:** Done\n---\n'
- fields: '**description:**\nTicket description content' (description non-null → displayName + ':\n' + val)
- comment block appended after a newline.

Full md = title + blockquote + '**Ticket:**...\n**Status:**...\n---\n' + md + '\n' + comments.

So for a comment {author: {displayName: 'Jane Doe'}, created: '2024-01-15T10:00:00.000+000', body: 'Looks good'}, comments section = '**Comments:**\n' + '> **Jane Doe** (2024-01-15):\n>\n> Looks good'.

Body with newline: body 'line1\nline2' → '> **Jane Doe** (2024-01-15):\n>\n> line1\n> line2'.

Author fallback: author {emailAddress: 'j@x.com'} → '> **j@x.com** (date):'. Author absent → '**Unknown**'. Created absent → '()'.

Empty comments array (or {total:0, comments: []}) → renderCommentsMarkdown returns '' → no '**Comments:**' in output.

Plain array shape: comment = [ {author...} ] → works too.

Multiple comments: blank line between: joined with '\n' → '> ...line1\n> ...line2'.

